% lps-converted-from: violations.lps
% This document was written from the LPS program violations.lps, which says the same thing in the older syntax. The two run alike, and tools/lps_to_le_test.pl checks that they do. The first line above is what keeps the older file from being read as this document's companion, which would run every rule twice.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 10.

the events are:
    *a thing* parks *a second thing*.
    *a thing* observeds violation *a second thing*; known as observed_violation.

the actions are:
    *a thing* issues fine *a second thing*; known as issue_fine.
    *a thing* tows; known as tow.
    *a thing* warns; known as warn.

the fluents are:
    *a thing* is parked *a second thing*; known as parked.
    *a thing* is fined *a second thing*; known as fined.
    the permit is *a thing*; known as permit.

the knowledge base violations includes:

initially the permit is resident.

when a thing parks a second thing
then the thing is parked the second thing.

when a thing issues fine a second thing
then the thing is fined the second thing.

it must not be true that
    me parks disabled_bay.

if a thing is parked disabled_bay at a time
    and it is not the case that the permit is the thing at the time
then the thing issues fine 70 from the time to a second time
    and the thing warns from the second time.

if a thing is fined a second thing
    and the thing is parked disabled_bay
then the thing tows.


scenario one is:
    visitor parks disabled_bay from 2 to 3.
